      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I got a bit carried away with the elven physicists. Alright, let's dive into the science.\n\nQuantum entanglement is a phenomenon where two or more particles become correlated in such a way that the state of one particle is dependent on the state of the other, even when they're separated by large distances. This means that measuring the state of one particle will instantly affect the state of the other, regardless of the distance between them.\n\nThe \"spooky\" aspect of entanglement comes from Einstein's famous quote, \"Spukhafte Fernwirkung\" or \"spooky action at a distance.\" He was skeptical of the idea that information could be transmitted between entangled particles instantaneously, which seemed to defy the fundamental principles of space and time.\n\nThe reason entanglement is considered \"spooky\" is that it appears to allow for faster-than-light communication, which is a fundamental aspect of special relativity. According to the theory of relativity, nothing can travel faster than the speed of light, and any attempt to communicate information faster than light would require a causal connection between the sender and receiver.\n\nHowever, entanglement doesn't actually allow for faster-than-light communication. Instead, it's a result of the non",
